  data: {
    LLM: "Don't play your King or Queen if they are part of a marriage until you have at least one trick won. You cannot declare the bonus points unless you have captured cards to put the bonus into.\n\nStock Management: In the first phase, discard your 7s and 8s to the table to 'fish' for Aces and 10s from the deck. The first phase is about hand optimization, not point capture.\n\nThe 'Closing' Bluff: If you suspect you have 66 points in hand (cards + declared marriages), you can 'close' the game. This stops all drawing. If you were right, you win; if not, your opponent gets a massive point bonus. Use this to stop an opponent who just drew a dangerous card.",
    Player: "Don't play your King or Queen if they are part of a marriage until you have at least one trick won. You cannot declare the bonus points unless you have captured cards to put the bonus into.\n\nStock Management: In the first phase, discard your 7s and 8s to the table to 'fish' for Aces and 10s from the deck. The first phase is about hand optimization, not point capture.\n\nThe 'Closing' Bluff: If you suspect you have 66 points in hand (cards + declared marriages), you can 'close' the game. This stops all drawing. If you were right, you win; if not, your opponent gets a massive point bonus. Use this to stop an opponent who just drew a dangerous card.",
